### Distributing Traffic Across Servers

A load balancer sits in front of your application servers and routes incoming requests.

#### Algorithms

```
Round Robin:        req1 → server1, req2 → server2, req3 → server3, req4 → server1...
Least Connections:  send to server with fewest active connections
IP Hash:            same client IP always routes to same server (sticky sessions)
Weighted:           server3 has 2x resources → gets 2x the traffic
```

#### Health Checks

```nginx
# nginx load balancer config
upstream app_servers {
  server app1.internal:3000;
  server app2.internal:3000;
  server app3.internal:3000;
}

server {
  location / {
    proxy_pass http://app_servers;
    health_check interval=5s uri=/health;
  }
}
```

```js
// Health check endpoint your app must expose
app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok', uptime: process.uptime() });
});
```

